mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;This course systematically covers the core content of pediatric nursing, including children's growth and development patterns and their influencing factors, child healthcare, prevention and nursing care of common pediatric diseases, and children's health management. Integrating theory with clinical practice, the course aims to help students master the fundamental knowledge and skills of pediatric nursing. It is designed to cultivate students' ability to promote family-centered child health and solve practical clinical problems. Meanwhile, by emphasizing humanistic care and communication skills, the course comprehensively enhances students' professional competencies in protecting and promoting children's physical and mental health.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
